{"reasoning": "The question has two parts: (1) who pays for the remedial actions needed to reach the cross-zonal capacity trajectory, and (2) how the cost-sharing methodology must treat redispatching with cross-border relevance.

Part 2: the context says the methodology shall include cost-sharing solutions for actions of cross-border relevance (Art. 74(2)), and that eligible costs must be determined transparently and auditably (Art. 74(3)). This part is answered.

Part 1: the context does not say who bears the costs of the remedial actions. Art. 74(b) says costs of redispatching or countertrading are shared between all TSOs of a capacity calculation region, but only for costs incurred to guarantee the firmness of cross-zonal capacity. Art. 16 of Regulation 2019/943 mentions a cost-sharing methodology, but its text is truncated and does not say who pays. Art. 16(13) in the actual regulation says costs are borne by the relevant TSOs, but that text is absent here. The link between the trajectory and the cost bearers is therefore not stated explicitly, so the answer is incomplete.", "sufficient": false, "confidence": 30}

