Question: Can a balancing service provider still update its balancing energy bid after gate closure?

Answer: No. The passages define 'balancing energy gate closure time' as the point in time when submission or update of a balancing energy bid for a standard product on a common merit order list is no longer permitted. After that time, balancing service providers are only required to report any unavailable volumes of their balancing energy bids to the connecting TSO (and to the DSO if required) without undue delay. The passages do not mention any exception allowing updates after gate closure.

