Question: Which technical parameters define a harmonised balancing energy bid, for instance how quickly the resource must reach full output?

Answer: A standard (harmonised) product's characteristics may include: preparation period, ramping period, full activation time (the time to full delivery), minimum and maximum quantity, deactivation period, minimum and maximum duration of delivery period, validity period and mode of activation (manual or automatic). Variable characteristics set by the balancing service provider are bid price, divisibility, location and minimum duration between the end of deactivation and the next activation. The corpus does not give numerical values, e.g. a specific full activation time; those are set in the list of standard products developed by TSOs.

