Question: Which body facilitates the regional procurement of balancing capacity, and what may it do as a last resort when the available remedial actions cannot deliver the minimum capacity?

Answer: Regional coordination centres facilitate the regional procurement of balancing capacity (Article 37(1)(k) of Regulation 2019/943). Where they conclude that the available remedial actions in or between capacity calculation regions are not sufficient to reach the linear trajectory or the 70% minimum capacities while respecting operational security limits, they may, as a measure of last resort, set out coordinated actions reducing the cross-zonal capacities accordingly (Article 16(3)). Transmission system operators may deviate from such coordinated actions only in accordance with Article 42(2).

