Answer: Regional coordination centres carry out the regional sizing of reserve capacity (Art. 37(1)(j) of Regulation 2019/943). Under Art. 6(7) of the same Regulation, TSOs perform the dimensioning of reserve capacity, facilitated at regional level. For FRR, all TSOs of an LFC block determine the positive reserve capacity on FRR, and it shall not be less than the positive dimensioning incident of the LFC block (Art. 157(2)(e) of Regulation 2017/1485). The corpus allows that capacity to be reduced through FRR sharing agreements, but the reduction is capped at 30% of the positive dimensioning incident in the CE and Nordic areas (Art. 157(2)(j)).

