Question: Which capacity mechanism has Poland introduced and what price cleared in its latest capacity auction?

Answer: The passages do not say which capacity mechanism Poland has introduced or what price cleared in its latest capacity auction. They only set out general rules: under Regulation 2019/943 Article 22, any capacity mechanism must be temporary, must not create undue market distortions or limit cross-zonal trade, must not go beyond what is necessary, and must select providers through a transparent, non-discriminatory and competitive process. Article 21 also bars Member States from introducing capacity mechanisms before the Commission has given an opinion on the implementation plan. None of this addresses Poland.

