Question: Can a balancing service provider still update its balancing energy bid after gate closure?

Answer: No. After the balancing energy gate closure time, balancing service providers are no longer permitted to submit or update their balancing energy bids. The gate closure time is defined as the point when submission or update of a balancing energy bid for a standard product on a common merit order list is no longer permitted. After that time, providers must only report any unavailable volumes of their bids to the connecting TSO (and to the DSO if required) without undue delay.

