Question: What criteria guide a TSO when choosing between possible grid-security countermeasures?

Answer: Article 21(2) says each TSO applies criteria when selecting remedial actions. The passages show two: (a) activate the most effective and economically efficient remedial actions, and (b) activate them as close as possible to real time, taking into account the expected activation time and the urgency of the situation. The passage ends after (b) with a semicolon, so the list may continue and I cannot confirm it is complete. Related provisions say a TSO may decide not to activate costly remedial actions for purely local constraints (Art. 23(5)). They also say TSOs must coordinate redispatching and countertrading of cross-border relevance (Reg. 2015/1222 Art. 35(4)).

